"# Aura Commerce Storefront
Status: IN_PROGRESS | Schema: v1
Last updated: 2026-03-05T14:30:00.000Z

## Goal

Build an open-source headless e-commerce storefront for artisanal pottery makers with local-first cart persistence and Stripe Checkout.

## Summary

Full-stack headless storefront utilizing Next.js App Router and Prisma ORM. Currently focusing on cart state synchronization and checkout session webhooks.

## Next Action

Finish the Stripe webhook endpoint in \`src/app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts\` to handle idempotency keys.

## Tech Stack

- **Next.js** (Frontend & API Routes, v14.2.0) — App Router architecture with React Server Components
- **TypeScript** (Language, v5.4.0) — Strict mode enabled throughout
- **Tailwind CSS** (Styling, v3.4.1) — Custom artisanal color palette and typography
- **Prisma** (Database ORM, v5.11.0) — PostgreSQL schema migrations and typed client
- **Stripe** (Payment Processing, v14.21.0) — Hosted checkout sessions with signed webhook verification

## Requirements

- [MUST] Catalog browsing must render server-side for optimal SEO and Core Web Vitals.
- [MUST] Cart items must persist across browser reloads without requiring user login.
- [SHOULD] Support discount coupon codes during the checkout initiation flow.
- [COULD] Customer order history lookup via email verification link.

## Decisions

### [ACTIVE] Use Stripe Hosted Checkout instead of custom payment element

*Date: 2026-03-02*

**Reason:** Reduces PCI compliance scope and simplifies mobile payment sheet integration.

### [ACTIVE] Store cart state in localStorage instead of server-side session cookies

*Date: 2026-03-03*

**Reason:** Allows completely anonymous browsing without database writes until checkout starts.

### [SUPERSEDED] Use SQLite for production catalog storage

*Date: 2026-03-01*

**Reason:** Initially considered for simplicity, but replaced by PostgreSQL for concurrent inventory transactions.

## Completed Work

- [x] PostgreSQL database schema for products, variants, and inventory levels.
- [x] Product detail pages with image gallery and variant selector.
- [x] Zustand cart store with localStorage synchronization.

## Tasks

- [ ] [DOING] [HIGH] Implement Stripe webhook handler for checkout.session.completed event.
- [ ] [TODO] [HIGH] Add inventory decrement transaction upon verified payment webhook.
- [ ] [TODO] [MEDIUM] Build order confirmation thank-you page with order summary.
- [ ] [BLOCKED] [MEDIUM] Setup Resend email notifications for customer receipts.

## Bugs & Issues

- [OPEN] [SEVERITY: MEDIUM] Rapid double-click on 'Add to Cart' button increments quantity twice.
- [OPEN] [SEVERITY: LOW] Cart badge badge count flashes 0 briefly during SSR hydration.
- [FIXED] [SEVERITY: HIGH] Product slug collation error on special characters.

## AI Instructions

- Always preserve strict TypeScript typing; never use \`any\`.
- Database mutations must execute inside explicit Prisma transactions.
- Do not log Stripe customer credentials, payment tokens, or webhook secrets.

## Open Questions

- Should inventory be reserved for 15 minutes when the customer enters Stripe Checkout?
- Do we require address verification for international shipping destinations?

## Project Files

- \`prisma/schema.prisma\` (2450 bytes, included) — Data model definitions for Products, Variants, Orders, and Customers.
- \`src/app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts\` (3820 bytes, included) — Webhook listener verifying Stripe signatures and processing payments.
- \`src/lib/cart-store.ts\` (1940 bytes, included) — Zustand client store managing local cart items and persistence.

## Attached Conversations

- **Stripe Webhook Idempotency Architecture** (claude, ~4200 tokens est., 12 messages, included)
- **Next.js App Router Cart Hydration Strategy** (chatgpt, ~2900 tokens est., 8 messages, excluded)
"
